nce": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Bill Cassidy (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Louisiana's open Senate seat favors Republicans by structure. The state leans about eleven points Republican, and Julia Letlow has far out-raised Democrat Jamie Davis while benefiting from millions in outside spending on both sides. Nearly every expert rater places the race in the Solid or Safe Republican column, and prediction markets give Davis only a five to nine percent chance of winning.\n\nThe main wrinkle is a late September poll from a Democratic-leaning sponsor showing Davis trailing by just four points, better than earlier summer polling. Even taking that at face value, the combination of state lean, money, and ratings makes a Davis upset a long shot. The race rates as Likely Republican with modest uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0491, "margin": -9.91}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0664, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0312, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0328, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0575, "margin": -9.0}]}